{
  "table": "screws",
  "about": "Thread sizes, mm. Clearance hole: ISO 273, medium fit is \"clearance_d\", the fine and coarse fits are listed beside it. Tap pilot: for a thread cut in metal; a thread in the print is a pilot of rules/tables/inserts.json and a named exception. Heads: cap DIN 912 / ISO 4762, button ISO 7380, countersunk DIN 7991 / ISO 10642 (diameter d, height h, hex key across flats). Counterbore diameter: DIN 974-1. Standard numbers are from the standards, not measured, unless a row says so.",
